This repository carries, and the binaries built from it embed, works of
others under their own terms:

- The fonts of fonts/data/: Ponomar, Indiction, Vertograd, Triodion,
  Cathisma, Oglavie, Pomorsky, Fedorovsk, Menaion and Monomakh, of the
  Ponomar Project (https://github.com/slavonic/), and Carlito
  (https://github.com/googlefonts/carlito, Reserved Font Name "Carlito"),
  each under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each font's copyright notice
  and the license are in fonts/data/OFL.txt.

- The Church Slavonic hyphenation patterns, cu/hyph-cu.txt: the pattern
  body of cu-tex's hyphenation/hyph-cu.tex (https://github.com/slavonic/cu-tex),
  Copyright (c) 2016 Aleksandr Andreev and Mike Kroutikov, under the MIT
  License, in cu/hyph-cu.LICENSE.txt. The kinovar red, #CC0803
  (cu/colors.go), is cu-tex's \cuKinovarColor.

- The ornaments of internal/assets/: from FreeSVG.org (https://freesvg.org)
  and PublicDomainVectors.org (https://publicdomainvectors.org), public
  domain, each chosen because its page there marked it so
  (internal/assets/svg/README.md).

The examples of examples/ and the README quote:

- Church Slavonic texts from cu-md-sandbox
  (https://github.com/slavonic/cu-md-sandbox), Copyright (c) 2018 Slavonic
  Computing Initiative, under the MIT License, in examples/cu/LICENSE.txt.
  The psalms of examples/cu/ are from its AugmentedPsalter1978. The
  samples of examples/styles.md and of the README are from the same book
  and from its Oktoih1981, Sluzhebnik1906, Chasoslov1991 and
  MineyaOctober1997. examples/psalm22.md adds the inscription of its psalm
  from the psalter, and examples/psalm22.png is that psalm's opening as
  this program sets it.

- English psalms from Sir Lancelot C. L. Brenton's translation of the
  Septuagint (1851), public domain, in the spelling of eBible.org's Updated
  Brenton English Septuagint (Adam Boyd, 2020, CC0).
